      "id": "oho91zj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.1 Western Ghats and Biodiversity"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Western Ghats is one of the world's eight 'hottest hotspots' of biological diversity and a UNESCO World Heritage Site.",
        "The Indian Elephant (Elephas maximus) is the official State Animal of Kerala.",
        "The Great Hornbill (Buceros bicornis) serves as the official State Bird of Kerala.",
        "Kanikonna (Cassia fistula) is the official State Flower, and the Coconut Palm is the State Tree of Kerala.",
        "Karimeen (Pearl Spot) was officially declared as the State Fish of Kerala in 2010."
      ],
      "id": "5tj2s8b"
    },
