    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ebqjqhn",
      "content": "The Western Ghats, also called the Sahyadri, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the eight 'hottest hot-spots' of biological diversity in the world. Kerala has about 29% of its geographical area under forest cover. The Gadgil Committee (2011) and Kasturirangan Committee (2013) have recommended environmental protection zones."
    },
